forms/**
run/**
var/**
envelop**
testdata/**
vendor/**
var/log/**
# Scratch output. A bare `tmp/` (no slash before a pattern) matches a tmp
# directory at ANY depth, so scripts/tmp and cmd/.../tmp are covered too —
# the earlier `tmp/**` was anchored to the repo root and let a nested tmp/
# through. No tracked file lives under a tmp/ path, so ignoring every one
# is safe. (git also cannot track an empty directory, so a stray empty
# tmp/ never reaches the index anyway; this is about the files put in it.)
tmp/
.aig*
.playwright-mcp/**
test_*
.continue/**
*.pad
*.pad.think
.env
webnote-go
*.log
webnote-linux-amd64-static
uploads/*
*.bak
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.*~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*OTP.png
*.tar
*.tgz
*.xz
*.lzma
*.zip
*.crt
*.key
*.sqlite3

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

*.swp
*.~
*.zip
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz
*.db
.vscode
models/.*
*.list

.aider*

# Signing links are one-time credentials. The CLI writes them beside the caller
# with mode 0600; ignoring the pattern keeps a careless `git add .` from putting
# a live token into history.
*.links.json
dist/**

# Python bytecode from running the scripts.
__pycache__/
